# VPS infrastructure state — this repo is PUBLIC.
# The full status report names the host, its public IP, the operator account and the path
# of its secrets file; committing it hands over a reconnaissance sheet. Antigravity writes
# the full report to *.private.md and keeps the redacted backend/vps/VPS_STATUS_REPORT.md
# (which IS committed) in sync. See .agent/rules/09-cross-agent-collaboration.md.
*.private.md

# Concrete forbidden strings for the secret-scan infra gate. Lives outside git on purpose:
# a denylist of infrastructure identifiers that was itself committed would publish the very
# values it exists to keep out. See eng/harness/check-secrets.ps1 part 4.
# Wildcard, not just .local.txt: CI must NOT materialise the denylist into a file at all (it
# is injected as $env:AUTOJMS_FORBIDDEN_VALUES), but a variant name such as
# forbidden-values.ci.txt is an easy accident and must not be commitable either.
eng/harness/forbidden-values*.txt
